# Docs travel with every GitHub push

Before `git push` of Meridian-lab changes, update the docs that the commit changes and include those edits in the same commit on `main`.

- `CHANGELOG.md` — a plain-language bullet for each user-visible change. Do not move the published release date unless that GitHub release asset was actually replaced.
- `README.md` — only if the short “what this is / how you use it” page would be wrong without the change.
- `docs/audio-analysis-pipeline.md` and `docs/placement-pipeline.md` — when listen or placement behavior changed.
- `docs/README.md` — when a guide’s promise changed.
- `POPULATE.md` — when setup facts (what lab `main` contains, how to open it) changed.

Write the behavior the code has now. Skip docs that the change does not touch. Push only after those updates are committed.
